From bad2ed0a5eb492abbcf3d1f010cde45e4117b5a1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fabio <fabio@git.it>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 14:18:33 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] task(T-A009): vfs: fix a slow directory listing blocking the
 listing of its parent (backport)

Backport of the fork's VFS patch for rclone/rclone#9643, carried as
webui/backports/01-vfs-list-without-lock.patch until upstream has a fix.

The VFS held the lock of a directory while it listed the remote. As
Dir.Name and Dir.Path take that lock, and listing the parent merges
each child directory under the child's lock, a slow or hung listing of
a directory also blocked the listings of its parents and every lookup
through it, for as long as the remote took to fail. With combine, one
unreachable upstream could block the root of the mount or of serve.

_readDir now releases the lock while it lists the remote, along the
lines discussed in #9644: a generation counter is incremented whenever
the cached contents change, and a listing is merged only if the path
and generation of the directory are unchanged, otherwise it is
discarded and redone. After 3 discarded listings the directory is
listed with the lock held, as before. Callers which need the directory
while it is being listed wait for that listing and share its result,
including its error.

The web interface docs no longer describe the blocking of the parent,
and TestParentPageWithHungChild checks that the page of a directory
doesn't wait for a subdirectory which hangs.

